1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,734
AI doesn't read words.

2
00:00:01,734 --> 00:00:02,907
It reads this.

3
00:00:02,907 --> 00:00:05,319
Before a language model sees your message,

4
00:00:05,319 --> 00:00:07,299
it chops the text into tokens:

5
00:00:07,299 --> 00:00:10,157
common chunks of letters, each turned into a number.

6
00:00:10,157 --> 00:00:12,294
"Strawberry" might become three pieces,

7
00:00:12,294 --> 00:00:14,523
like "str", "aw" and "berry".

8
00:00:14,523 --> 00:00:16,974
The model never sees the individual letters.

9
00:00:16,974 --> 00:00:19,055
So when you ask how many R's it has,

10
00:00:19,055 --> 00:00:21,182
it's reasoning about chunks, not spelling.

11
00:00:21,182 --> 00:00:23,233
Newer models often work around this,

12
00:00:23,233 --> 00:00:24,838
but the letters were never what it saw.
